# Echo & The Bunnymen and Happy Mondays announce joint 2027 UK ‘greatest hits’ tour

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from NME Music Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Music News Echo & The Bunnymen and Happy Mondays announce joint 2027 UK ‘greatest hits’ tour Dates include a stop at London’s O2 Brixton Academy and two shows in Edinburgh By Liberty Dunworth | 27th November 2026 Ian McCulloch of Echo and The Bunnymen and Shaun Ryder of Happy Mondays. CREDIT: Gus Stewart and Dave Simpson/Getty

Echo & The Bunnymen and Happy Mondays are joining forces for a UK ‘greatest hits’ co-headline tour.

The two bands are set to hit the road together next spring, playing six shows across the country to celebrate the biggest hits from their respective careers. The tour kicks off on May 7 with an opening night at The Prospect Building in Bristol.

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

From there, they’ll make stops at Manchester’s O2 Apollo, London’s O2 Academy Brixton and Liverpool’s M&S Bank Arena on May 8, 14 and 15 respectively, before wrapping things up with two shows in Scotland. Those take place on May 22 and 23, and will be held at the Usher Hall in Edinburgh.

Tickets go on sale on Friday December 4 at 9am GMT. Visit here for tickets and more information.

